{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Kafka + Avro Live Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook validates:\n",
        "\n",
        "`Python producer \u2192 Confluent Schema Registry \u2192 Kafka \u2192 Databricks \u2192 Confluent framing \u2192 Avro decode \u2192 event reconciliation`\n",
        "\n",
        "**Pass criteria**\n",
        "- Databricks can read `telehealth_analytics`.\n",
        "- Magic byte is `00`.\n",
        "- Schema ID matches the Registry ID from the producer run.\n",
        "- The decoded `event_id` matches one `ACKNOWLEDGED` record in `delivery-report.json`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Bronze ingestion, checkpoints, watermarking, and deduplication are intentionally left for Day 7.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 0. Before running\n",
        "\n",
        "From `data/day-06-live-01/delivery-report.json`, choose one `ACKNOWLEDGED` delivery and copy its:\n",
        "- `event_id`\n",
        "- `partition`\n",
        "- `offset`\n",
        "\n",
        "Keep Kafka credentials in Databricks Secrets. Do not hard-code them in this notebook.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Parameters\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"topic\", \"telehealth_analytics\")\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"secret_scope\", \"telehealth\")\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"bootstrap_secret_key\", \"kafka-bootstrap-servers\")\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"api_key_secret_key\", \"kafka-api-key\")\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"api_secret_secret_key\", \"kafka-api-secret\")\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"expected_schema_id\", \"100001\")\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"expected_event_id\", \"\")\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"expected_partition\", \"\")\n",
        "dbutils.widgets.text(\"expected_offset\", \"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "TOPIC = dbutils.widgets.get(\"topic\").strip()\n",
        "SECRET_SCOPE = dbutils.widgets.get(\"secret_scope\").strip()\n",
        "BOOTSTRAP_SECRET_KEY = dbutils.widgets.get(\"bootstrap_secret_key\").strip()\n",
        "API_KEY_SECRET_KEY = dbutils.widgets.get(\"api_key_secret_key\").strip()\n",
        "API_SECRET_SECRET_KEY = dbutils.widgets.get(\"api_secret_secret_key\").strip()\n",
        "EXPECTED_SCHEMA_ID = int(dbutils.widgets.get(\"expected_schema_id\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_EVENT_ID = dbutils.widgets.get(\"expected_event_id\").strip()\n",
        "partition_raw = dbutils.widgets.get(\"expected_partition\").strip()\n",
        "offset_raw = dbutils.widgets.get(\"expected_offset\").strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "if not EXPECTED_EVENT_ID or not partition_raw or not offset_raw:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"Fill expected_event_id, expected_partition, and expected_offset from delivery-report.json.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_PARTITION = int(partition_raw)\n",
        "EXPECTED_OFFSET = int(offset_raw)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Validation target\")\n",
        "print(\" topic:\", TOPIC)\n",
        "print(\" schema_id:\", EXPECTED_SCHEMA_ID)\n",
        "print(\" event_id:\", EXPECTED_EVENT_ID)\n",
        "print(\" partition:\", EXPECTED_PARTITION)\n",
        "print(\" offset:\", EXPECTED_OFFSET)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Build the Kafka connection\n",
        "\n",
        "Databricks uses shaded Kafka classes. With SASL/PLAIN, use the `kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka...PlainLoginModule` class.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "kafka_bootstrap_servers = dbutils.secrets.get(\n",
        "    scope=SECRET_SCOPE,\n",
        "    key=BOOTSTRAP_SECRET_KEY,\n",
        ")\n",
        "kafka_api_key = dbutils.secrets.get(\n",
        "    scope=SECRET_SCOPE,\n",
        "    key=API_KEY_SECRET_KEY,\n",
        ")\n",
        "kafka_api_secret = dbutils.secrets.get(\n",
        "    scope=SECRET_SCOPE,\n",
        "    key=API_SECRET_SECRET_KEY,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "kafka_options = {\n",
        "    \"kafka.bootstrap.servers\": kafka_bootstrap_servers,\n",
        "    \"kafka.security.protocol\": \"SASL_SSL\",\n",
        "    \"kafka.sasl.mechanism\": \"PLAIN\",\n",
        "    \"kafka.sasl.jaas.config\": (\n",
        "        \"kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka.common.security.plain.\"\n",
        "        \"PlainLoginModule required \"\n",
        "        f'username=\"{kafka_api_key}\" '\n",
        "        f'password=\"{kafka_api_secret}\";'\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Kafka options prepared without printing credentials.\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Read the topic as a bounded batch\n",
        "\n",
        "Day 6 is a one-time validation, so use `spark.read`. Day 7 will move to `spark.readStream`.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "raw_df = (\n",
        "    spark.read\n",
        "        .format(\"kafka\")\n",
        "        .options(**kafka_options)\n",
        "        .option(\"subscribe\", TOPIC)\n",
        "        .option(\"startingOffsets\", \"earliest\")\n",
        "        .option(\"endingOffsets\", \"latest\")\n",
        "        .load()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Kafka batch reader created.\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Inspect transport metadata\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not cast `value` to string. It contains Confluent-framed binary Avro.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from pyspark.sql import functions as F\n",
        "\n",
        "inspection_df = (\n",
        "    raw_df\n",
        "    .select(\n",
        "        \"topic\",\n",
        "        \"partition\",\n",
        "        \"offset\",\n",
        "        \"timestamp\",\n",
        "        F.length(\"value\").alias(\"value_length\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .orderBy(\"partition\", \"offset\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(inspection_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "assert inspection_df.limit(1).count() == 1, \"No Kafka records were returned.\"\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Locate the acknowledged record\n",
        "\n",
        "Kafka records are uniquely located by topic + partition + offset.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "target_raw = (\n",
        "    raw_df\n",
        "    .filter(\n",
        "        (F.col(\"partition\") == EXPECTED_PARTITION)\n",
        "        & (F.col(\"offset\") == EXPECTED_OFFSET)\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "target_count = target_raw.count()\n",
        "assert target_count == 1, (\n",
        "    f\"Expected exactly one record at partition={EXPECTED_PARTITION}, \"\n",
        "    f\"offset={EXPECTED_OFFSET}, but found {target_count}.\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    target_raw.select(\n",
        "        \"topic\",\n",
        "        \"partition\",\n",
        "        \"offset\",\n",
        "        \"timestamp\",\n",
        "        F.length(\"value\").alias(\"value_length\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Inspect the 5-byte Confluent framing header\n",
        "\n",
        "Wire format:\n",
        "\n",
        "`[1 byte magic=0] [4 bytes big-endian schema ID] [Avro datum...]`\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "header_df = (\n",
        "    target_raw\n",
        "    .select(\n",
        "        \"topic\",\n",
        "        \"partition\",\n",
        "        \"offset\",\n",
        "        F.length(\"value\").alias(\"value_length\"),\n",
        "        F.hex(F.substring(\"value\", 1, 1)).alias(\"magic_hex\"),\n",
        "        F.hex(F.substring(\"value\", 2, 4)).alias(\"schema_id_hex\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .withColumn(\n",
        "        \"schema_id\",\n",
        "        F.conv(F.col(\"schema_id_hex\"), 16, 10).cast(\"long\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(header_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "header = header_df.first()\n",
        "assert header[\"value_length\"] > 5, \"Kafka value contains no Avro body.\"\n",
        "assert header[\"magic_hex\"] == \"00\", f\"Unexpected magic byte: {header['magic_hex']}\"\n",
        "assert header[\"schema_id\"] == EXPECTED_SCHEMA_ID, (\n",
        "    f\"Schema ID mismatch: expected {EXPECTED_SCHEMA_ID}, got {header['schema_id']}\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Confluent framing header: PASS\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Strip the framing header\n",
        "\n",
        "Spark `substring` is 1-based, so the Avro body begins at byte 6.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "framed_df = (\n",
        "    target_raw\n",
        "    .withColumn(\"magic_hex\", F.hex(F.substring(\"value\", 1, 1)))\n",
        "    .withColumn(\"schema_id_hex\", F.hex(F.substring(\"value\", 2, 4)))\n",
        "    .withColumn(\n",
        "        \"schema_id\",\n",
        "        F.conv(F.col(\"schema_id_hex\"), 16, 10).cast(\"long\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .withColumn(\n",
        "        \"avro_body\",\n",
        "        F.expr(\"substring(value, 6, length(value) - 5)\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    framed_df.select(\n",
        "        \"partition\",\n",
        "        \"offset\",\n",
        "        \"magic_hex\",\n",
        "        \"schema_id\",\n",
        "        F.length(\"value\").alias(\"full_length\"),\n",
        "        F.length(\"avro_body\").alias(\"avro_body_length\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Load the Avro V1 schema\n",
        "\n",
        "This embedded schema mirrors `contracts/events/clickstream_event_v1.avsc`.\n",
        "\n",
        "For a later production refactor, load that `.avsc` file directly from the checked-out repo to keep one schema source of truth.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "schema_json = r'''\n",
        "{\n",
        "  \"type\": \"record\",\n",
        "  \"name\": \"TelehealthClickstreamEvent\",\n",
        "  \"namespace\": \"com.telehealth.analytics.clickstream.v1\",\n",
        "  \"doc\": \"Synthetic product analytics event. Contains no clinical or protected health information.\",\n",
        "  \"fields\": [\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"event_id\", \"type\": \"string\", \"doc\": \"Immutable business-event identifier. Retries reuse this value.\"},\n",
        "    {\n",
        "      \"name\": \"event_name\",\n",
        "      \"type\": {\n",
        "        \"type\": \"enum\",\n",
        "        \"name\": \"EventName\",\n",
        "        \"symbols\": [\n",
        "          \"specialty_searched\",\n",
        "          \"provider_profile_viewed\",\n",
        "          \"appointment_slot_viewed\",\n",
        "          \"booking_started\",\n",
        "          \"appointment_booked\",\n",
        "          \"checkin_started\",\n",
        "          \"waiting_room_entered\",\n",
        "          \"video_visit_started\",\n",
        "          \"video_connection_failed\",\n",
        "          \"visit_completed\"\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "      }\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"event_time\", \"type\": {\"type\": \"long\", \"logicalType\": \"timestamp-micros\"}},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"received_at\", \"type\": {\"type\": \"long\", \"logicalType\": \"timestamp-micros\"}},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"anonymous_id\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"customer_id\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"session_id\", \"type\": \"string\"},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"booking_journey_id\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"appointment_id\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n",
        "    {\n",
        "      \"name\": \"scheduled_start_time\",\n",
        "      \"type\": [\"null\", {\"type\": \"long\", \"logicalType\": \"timestamp-micros\"}],\n",
        "      \"default\": null\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"provider_id\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"device_type\", \"type\": \"string\"},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"platform\", \"type\": \"string\"},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"specialty\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n",
        "    {\"name\": \"schema_version\", \"type\": \"int\", \"default\": 1}\n",
        "  ]\n",
        "}\n",
        "'''\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Avro schema loaded.\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8. Decode the Avro datum\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from pyspark.sql.avro.functions import from_avro\n",
        "\n",
        "decoded_df = (\n",
        "    framed_df\n",
        "    .filter(F.col(\"magic_hex\") == \"00\")\n",
        "    .filter(F.col(\"schema_id\") == EXPECTED_SCHEMA_ID)\n",
        "    .select(\n",
        "        \"topic\",\n",
        "        \"partition\",\n",
        "        \"offset\",\n",
        "        \"schema_id\",\n",
        "        from_avro(F.col(\"avro_body\"), schema_json).alias(\"event\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "event_df = (\n",
        "    decoded_df\n",
        "    .select(\n",
        "        \"topic\",\n",
        "        \"partition\",\n",
        "        \"offset\",\n",
        "        \"schema_id\",\n",
        "        \"event.*\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    event_df.select(\n",
        "        \"topic\",\n",
        "        \"partition\",\n",
        "        \"offset\",\n",
        "        \"schema_id\",\n",
        "        \"event_id\",\n",
        "        \"event_name\",\n",
        "        \"event_time\",\n",
        "        \"received_at\",\n",
        "        \"customer_id\",\n",
        "        \"session_id\",\n",
        "        \"provider_id\",\n",
        "        \"device_type\",\n",
        "        \"platform\",\n",
        "        \"schema_version\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 9. Reconcile with `delivery-report.json`\n",
        "\n",
        "This proves that the exact Kafka record acknowledged by the producer decodes to the same business `event_id` in Databricks.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "verification_row = (\n",
        "    event_df\n",
        "    .select(\n",
        "        \"event_id\",\n",
        "        \"event_name\",\n",
        "        \"partition\",\n",
        "        \"offset\",\n",
        "        \"schema_id\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .first()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "assert verification_row is not None, \"Decoded event was not produced.\"\n",
        "assert verification_row[\"event_id\"] == EXPECTED_EVENT_ID, (\n",
        "    f\"Event ID mismatch: expected {EXPECTED_EVENT_ID}, \"\n",
        "    f\"got {verification_row['event_id']}\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "assert verification_row[\"partition\"] == EXPECTED_PARTITION\n",
        "assert verification_row[\"offset\"] == EXPECTED_OFFSET\n",
        "assert verification_row[\"schema_id\"] == EXPECTED_SCHEMA_ID\n",
        "\n",
        "result = {\n",
        "    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n",
        "    \"topic\": TOPIC,\n",
        "    \"event_id\": verification_row[\"event_id\"],\n",
        "    \"event_name\": verification_row[\"event_name\"],\n",
        "    \"partition\": verification_row[\"partition\"],\n",
        "    \"offset\": verification_row[\"offset\"],\n",
        "    \"schema_id\": verification_row[\"schema_id\"],\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"DAY 6 LIVE GATE: PASS\")\n",
        "print(result)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Result\n",
        "\n",
        "A final `LIVE GATE: PASS` proves:\n",
        "1. Databricks authenticated to Kafka.\n",
        "2. The producer-reported Kafka record was found.\n",
        "3. The Confluent framing header was valid.\n",
        "4. The schema ID matched.\n",
        "5. The Avro payload decoded successfully.\n",
        "6. The decoded `event_id` matched `delivery-report.json`.\n",
        "\n",
      ]
    }
  ],
